gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0058640701439672815,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":37.7,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.01564492775172277,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":17.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0809695827318375,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.06122253468173633,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00794411724421312,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.01887,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Genworth Financial, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides mortgage and long-term care insurance products in the United States. It operates through two segments: Enact and Closed Block. The company offers primary mortgage, and mortgage insurance products, and contract underwriting services. It also provides long-term care insurance products that are intended to protect against the significant and escalating costs of long-term care services provided in the insured's home, assisted living, and nursing facilities. In addition, the company offers protection and retirement income products, that includes traditional and non-traditional life insurance, such as term, universal and term universal life insurance, corporate-owned life insurance, and funding agreements; fixed annuities; and variable annuities. It distributes its products through sales force, sales representatives, and digital marketing programs. Genworth Financial, Inc. was founded in 1871 and is headquartered in Glen Allen, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas Joseph McInerney | President, CEO & Director | Age 68 | Compensation: $4.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $2.4M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $19K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Genworth Financial Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.1B market cap on $7.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 91% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9138728869581638},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 28% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Genworth Financial (GNW) a Great Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026380/is-genworth-financial-gnw-a-great-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_2-3026380","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794231602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (GNW) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/Trading_S